= Complex system — Simple =

A '''complex system''' has parts that interact in ways that strongly affect what the whole system does.

The important part is not just having many pieces.

Interactions can create feedback, adaptation, networks, and new larger patterns.

Examples include ecosystems, brains, economies, and power grids.

A complex system is not simply the same thing as a complicated machine.

